# The enforcement surface. Replace @OWNER with a real human owner and enable
# "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch; that host
# setting is what makes AGENTS.md's "loosening requires human countersign"
# mechanical instead of advisory. Directory.Build.props,
# Directory.Packages.props, and .editorconfig are unanchored on purpose:
# MSBuild and the analyzers resolve them nearest-first, so a nested copy
# shadows the wall. If the mise task fragment (20-csharp.toml) lives outside
# /.config/mise/, add its path here.
.editorconfig @OWNER
/.config/dotnet-tools.json @OWNER
/.config/mise/ @OWNER
/.github/ @OWNER
/AGENTS.md @OWNER
/BannedSymbols.txt @OWNER
Directory.Build.props @OWNER
Directory.Packages.props @OWNER
/global.json @OWNER
/stryker-config.json @OWNER
